  "english": "29. Monday, Tone 8 [DK]. Saint Stephen of Ulnia, and others. Canticle [Harts], Tone 4 [BK]: \"We bless You, Lord\" (Orhnemk uzkez Ter).\n\nSeptember.\n4. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts], Tone 6 [GK]: \"Ineffable\" (Anchareli). Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [GK]: \"The Divine\" (Zastvadsayin). Barekendan [fast] of the Holy Cross.\n5. Monday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Fast. Canticle of the Fast [Harts aghts], Tone 4 [BK]: \"Blessed are You, Lord, God of our fathers\" (Hartsun merots orhneal es Ter).\n8. Thursday, Tone 2 [AK]. Of the Fast. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\n11. Sunday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Feast of the Elevation of the Holy Cross [Khachverats]. See up to the Fourteenth Sunday in the First Volume, maintaining the order of the place.\n18. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Second [Sunday]. Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 4 [BK]: \"Christ is risen\" (Kristos yareav). Barekendan [fast] of the Cross of Varag.\n19. Monday, Tone 5 [GDZ]. Fast. Saint Mamas, and others. Canticle [Harts], Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who in the battle\" (Ork i marti).\n21. Wednesday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Canticle of the Fast [Harts aghts], Tone 4 [BK]: \"Lord God of our fathers\" (Ter astvads hartsun merots).\n25. Sunday, Tone 3 [BZ]. Third [Sunday]. Feast of the Cross of Varag. The intervening period of eating is eight weeks.\n\nOctober.\n2. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [AK]: \"Risen\" (Yarutsial).\n9. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Fifth [Sunday]. Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [ADZ]: \"Glory of Your resurrection, Lord\" (Park yarutian ko Ter), and \"With the women\" (Und kanaysn).\n16. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 8 [DK]: \"When they came\" (Yorzham ekin), and \"The angel descended\" (Ej hreshtakn), and \"The choirs of angels\" (Hreshtakatsn dasnk).\n23. Sunday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Seventh [Sunday]. Discovery of the Cross [Gyut Khach].\n25. Tuesday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Saint Hyperichius and companions [Hiperikiants]. Canticle [Harts], Tone 4 [BK]: \"We bless You\" (Orhnemk uzkez).\n26. Wednesday, Tone 2 [AK]. Canticle [Harts], Tone 5 [GZ]: \"God of our fathers\" (Hartsun merots astvads).\n30. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK]. Eighth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts], Tone 8 [DK]: \"Who [revealed] Your all-powerful power\" (Or zamenazor zorutiund). Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [GK]: \"Your resurrection\" (Zko yarutiund).\n\nNovember.\n6. Sunday, Tone 5 [GDZ]. Ninth [Sunday]. Nocturn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [GDZ]: \"The Myrrh-bearers\" (Yughaber), and \"Today the resurrection\" (Aysor yarutiun), and \"Cross-bearing\" (Khachanish).",
